cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GnosisLab-VM — isolated KVM lab for agentic ML experimentation"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bikeyev
    given-names: Alexander
    affiliation: Cloudcell Limited
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.0.2"
date-released: 2026-10-14
repository-code: "https://github.com/cloudcell/gnosislab-vm"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/buckets/cloudcell/LabLoop"
abstract: >-
  GnosisLab-VM is a secure, reproducible, per-user experimentation lab for
  agentic ML work: an isolated KVM/libvirt VM containing VSCodium with
  AI coding agents, a trusted zone of scientific-state MCP services
  (agora, arete, zetesis, episteme, anamnesis), and a hostile zone for
  controlled execution of generated or untrusted experiment code —
  with rootless Podman, pull-only extraction and push-only ingest
  channels over the QEMU guest agent, and a frozen, clonable template
  built unattended from a Linux Mint ISO.
keywords:
  - machine-learning
  - sandboxing
  - reproducibility
  - KVM
  - MCP
  - experiment-management
